</tbody>
</table>
</span></div>
</figure>
</section>
<section id="A9" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix I </span>Study on “EF+LSG” setting</h2>

<div id="A9.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A9.p1.1" class="ltx_p">To demonstrate the novelty and effectiveness of our LSG method, we provide additional ablation studies in the “EF+LSG” setting, as shown in the Table <a href="#A8.T4" title="Table D ‣ Appendix H More Details of token-level supervision. ‣ Bilateral Collaboration with Large Vision-Language Models forOpen Vocabulary Human-Object Interaction Detection" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">D</span></a>. In the “EF+LSG w/o <math id="A9.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{A}_{\text{f}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝑨</mi><mtext>f</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{A}_{\text{f}}</annotation></semantics></math>” setting, we remove the influence of <math id="A9.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{A}_{\text{f}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝑨</mi><mtext>f</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{A}_{\text{f}}</annotation></semantics></math>, and the model performance drops to 30.62%/33.10%/32.57% on Unseen/Seen/Full in the UC-NF setting.
This demonstrates that LSG enhances the performance by optimizing the attention maps generated by the model. In the “EF+LSG w/o (<math id="A9.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{A}_{\text{f}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝑨</mi><mtext>f</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{A}_{\text{f}}</annotation></semantics></math> and LLM)” setting, we remove both <math id="A9.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{A}_{\text{f}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝑨</mi><mtext>f</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{A}_{\text{f}}</annotation></semantics></math> and LLM from “EF+LSG” and retain the learnable <math id="A9.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{Q}^{\text{q}}_{\text{f}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>𝑸</mi><mtext>f</mtext><mtext>q</mtext></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{Q}^{\text{q}}_{\text{f}}</annotation></semantics></math>. Compared with the performance of “EF+LSG”, the performance drops by 0.99%/1.13%/1.28% on Unseen/Seen/Full in the UC-NF setting.
This means LSG mainly benefits from its LLM supervision instead of refined-query <math id="A9.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{Q}^{\text{q}}_{\text{f}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>𝑸</mi><mtext>f</mtext><mtext>q</mtext></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{Q}^{\text{q}}_{\text{f}}</annotation></semantics></math>, which requires the HOI detector to provide high-quality attention bias <math id="A9.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{A}_{\text{f}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝑨</mi><mtext>f</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{A}_{\text{f}}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</section>
</article>
